TI  - ETHYLENE EMISSION BY A DECIDUOUS TREE, TILIA-AMERICANA, IN RESPONSE TO FEEDING BY INTRODUCED BASSWOOD THRIPS, THRIPS-CALCARATUS
T2  - JOURNAL OF CHEMICAL ECOLOGY
AB  - Ethylene emission from excised and intact American basswood tissue was increased after seedlings were infested with the bud-feeding herbivore, Thrips calcaratus. Gas chromatographic analysis showed that thrips-infested tissue produced significantly more ethylene than mechanically damaged or control tissue. The possibility that thrips feeding enhances ethylene-mediated stress signals is discussed.
