TI  - High Reflectance Nanoscale V/Sc Multilayer for Soft X-ray Water Window Region
T2  - SCIENTIFIC REPORTS
AB  - V/Sc multilayer is experimentally demonstrated for the first time as a high reflectance mirror for the soft X-ray water window region. It primarily works at above the Sc-L edge (lambda = 3.11 nm) under near normal incidence while a second peak appears at above the V-L edge (lambda = 2.42 nm) under grazing incidence. The V/Sc multilayer fabricated with a d-spacing of 1.59 nm and 30 bilayers has a smaller interface width (sigma = 0.27 and 0.32 nm) than the conventional used Cr/Sc (sigma = 0.28 and 0.47 nm). For V/Sc multilayer with 30 bilayers, the introduction of B4C barrier layers has little improvement on the interface structure. As the number of bilayers increasing to 400, the growth morphology and microstructure of the V/Sc layers evolves with slightly increased crystallization. Nevertheless, the surface roughness remains to be 0.25 nm. A maximum soft X-ray reflectance of 18.4% is measured at lambda = 3.129 nm at 9 degrees off-normal incidence using the 400-bilayers V/Sc multilayer. According to the fitted model, an s-polarization reflectance of 5.2% can also be expected at lambda = 2.425 nm under 40 degrees incidence. Based on the promising experimental results, further improvement of the reflectance can be achieved by using a more stable deposition system, exploring different interface engineering methods and so on.
